Combining Columns in a Data Table







    Scenarios

    In the data table display scenario, when multiple rows or columns share the same data record, these rows or columns can be combined.




    Implementation Method

    The setSpanMethod method is added to the data table. The input parameter of the method is an object, which contains the following properties: row (current row), column (current column), rowIndex (current row No.), and columnIndex (current column No.). This function can return an array containing two elements with the first one indicating rowspan and the second one indicating colspan. Alternatively, this function can return an object whose key name is rowspan and colspan. The business side can implement this function based on its own requirements.




    Example

    U.ready(function () {
    let id = "removeAllColumns";
    let eventName = "click";
    let tableData = [];
    let tableColumn = [];
    let callback = function () {
        let spanMethod = function ({ row, column, rowIndex, columnIndex }) {
            let tempDataIndex = tableColumn[columnIndex - 1];
            if(!tempDataIndex) {
                return [1, 1];
            }
            if(tableData[rowIndex - 1] && tableData[rowIndex][tempDataIndex] === tableData[rowIndex - 1][tempDataIndex]) {
                return [0, 0];
            }
            let tempIndex = 1;
            while(tableData[rowIndex + tempIndex] && tableData[rowIndex][tempDataIndex] === tableData[rowIndex + tempIndex][tempDataIndex]) {
                tempIndex ++;
            }
            return [tempIndex, 1]
        };
        S("datagrid").setSpanMethod(spanMethod);
    }
    Spl.EventBus.register(id, eventName, callback);
});





