Configuring the Customized Data Export Service







    Prerequisites

    The script service for exporting customized data has been configured.




    Context

    When a user views data on the front end, there is a scenario where the user needs to export the data as an offline file and store or transfer the file locally.

    Therefore, during app development, the data export capability is supported. You can configure the data export service and use the export button for page development to implement the overall export capability.

    Customized data export is a method of using a script to define information such as the export format and fields.




    Procedure


     Choose Project Management.

     Select the project and module to be operated.

     Configure the service for which the customized data export function is required.



       Choose Service.

       Click  to create a service. Specify Service Name and use the blank template.

       Drag RunScript from the left pane.

       Click  to edit node properties.

       In the Selecting a script area, click Edit.

       Set the script content Developers need to define scripts based on export requirements. The following is an example. Save the configuration.

         Example of exporting an Excel file:
          var request = {};
request.user = 'default_admin';                                 // Set an existing proxy user. This parameter is optional.
request.type = 'default_excel';                                 // The default export type is Excel.
request.fileName = "export_file_name";                         // Name of the exported file
request.encryptExport = false;                                  // Whether data is exported in encrypted mode
request.templates=["xxx/xxx/xxx"];                             // Template list
request.start=0;                                                // Starting point for query
request.total=10;                                               // Limitations on quantity
