Fault Element Can Be Returned to the Northbound Client






   The API Fabric cannot properly parse the value of Fault returned by the southbound service. You can customize a JavaScript script in the exception diagram element to return the value of Fault in the SOAP packet to the northbound client.


    Overview

    When the values of the subelements such as faultcode, faultstring, and detail in Fault are returned to the northbound client, JavaScript must be compiled in the exception diagram element and the subelement values cannot be bypassed.

    When the values of faultcode and faultstring are empty, the value of detail can be returned.




    Constraint


     Namespaces cannot be carried in Fault.

     Bypass APIs are not supported.
      You cannot use bypass type for southbound APIs that return the Fault element. Bypass APIs do not require flow orchestration and cannot use the exception diagram element.






    Examples


     In this document, SOAP 1.2 is used as an example:
     <env:Envelope xmlns:env="http://www.w3.org/2003/05/soap-envelope">
 <env:Header/>
 <env:Body>
 <env:Fault>
    <env:Code>
       <env:Value>env:Sender</env:Value>
    </env:Code>
    <env:Reason>
          <env:Text xml:lang="en-US">
          fault message
         </env:Text>
    </env:Reason>
     <env:Role>
        http://gizmos.com/order
     </env:Role>
      <env:Detail></env:Detail>
 </env:Fault>
 </env:Body>
 </env:Envelope>





    JavaScript Example

    The Fault packet structure in SOAP 1.1 is different from that in SOAP 1.2. You need to compile the JavaScript script for obtaining Fault information based on the specific protocol version.


     An example of JavaScript (SOAP 1.2) is as follows:
     /**
* Define a function based on the following template:
* The function name'Demo'and the parameters 'param1' and 'param2'can be changed as required
*/
function getFaultBody(__headers, _exception) {
         if (_exception && _exception.serviceSoapEnvelope && JSON.stringify(_exception.serviceSoapEnvelope) !== {}){
                   var envelope = _exception.serviceSoapEnvelope;
                   response = {};
                   response.error = {};
                   if(envelope.getBody() && envelope.getBody().getFault()){
                            var getFault = envelope.getBody().getFault();
                            if (getFault.getCode() !== undefined && getFault.getCode() !== null){
                                     response.error.faultcode = _exception.serviceSoapEnvelope.getBody().getFault().getCode().getText();
                            }
                            if (getFault.getReason() !== undefined && getFault.getReason() !== null){
                                     response.error.faultstring = _exception.serviceSoapEnvelope.getBody().getFault().getReason().getText();
                            }
                            if (getFault.getDetail() && getFault.getDetail().getFirstOMChild()){
                                     response.error.detail = getFault.getDetail().getFirstOMChild();
                            }
                            if (_exception.cause){
                                     response.error.cause = _exception.cause;
                            }
                   }
                   return response;
         }else{
                   var _Fault = _exception && _exception.cause;
                   var _FaultDetail = _Fault && _Fault.faultMessage;
                   var _result = {
                            headers: __headers,
                            error: {
                                     faultcode: _Fault.faultCode || "soapenv:Server",
                                     faultstring: _Fault.detailMessage,
                                     faultactor: _Fault.faultRole,
                                     detail: {}
                            }
                   };
                   if (_FaultDetail) {
                            var _FaultDetailTypes = ["clientException", "serverException", "MessageFault"];
                            for (var i in _FaultDetailTypes) {
                                     var _FaultDetailType = _FaultDetailTypes[i];
                                     if (_FaultDetail[_FaultDetailType]) {
                                               _result.error.detail[_FaultDetailType] = getAAFaultDetail(_exception);
                                     }
                            }
                   }
                   return _result;
         }
};









