Generating an SMPP Definition File






   The develop-state API Fabric supports the function of generating APIs by importing SMPP definition files and configuring policies on the page.

   This section describes how to generate an SMPP definition file.


    Context

    The develop-state API Fabric bears the SMPP protocol through the RPC protocol to implement data forwarding and exchange.




    Prerequisites


     You have installed local environment where the protoc is installed. For details, see the Proto official website.

     The .proto file has been prepared. The file template is as follows.



        Set request parameters and response parameters based on site requirements during file creation. The parameters cannot be modified after the SMPP definition file is generated.





      // The current system only supports proto3

syntax = "proto3";

package simpleService;

message SearchRequest {    //Define request parameters.
 string query = 1;
 int32 page_number = 2;
 int32 result_per_page = 3;
 Corpus corpus = 4;
}

enum Corpus {      //Enumerated type
 UNIVERSAL = 0;
 WEB = 1;
 IMAGES = 2;
 LOCAL = 3;
 NEWS = 4;
 PRODUCTS = 5;
 VIDEO = 6;
}

message SearchResponse {     //Define response parameters.
 repeated Result results = 1;
}

message Result {
 string url = 1;
 string title = 2;
 repeated string snippets = 3;
}

service SearchService {    //SearchService indicates the service name, which can be customized.
 rpc Search (SearchRequest) returns (SearchResponse);
}






    Procedure


     Generate an SMPP definition file.



       Run the cmd command in the local environment.

       Run the following command in the command prompt to generate the .desc file:
        protoc -I={Local path for storing the .proto file} --descriptor_set_out={Local path for storing the .proto file}\{SMPP definition file name}.desc {Local path for storing the .proto file}\{.proto file name}.proto





     Pack the SMPP definition file.


      Compress the .desc and .proto files generated in step 1 into a .zip package.



     Upload the SMPP definition file.



       When the SMPP functions as a client, upload the package on the Develop API page. For details, see Adding an API.

       If the SMPP functions as the server, upload the file on the Endpoint Management page. For details, see Adding an Endpoint.














