Exception Diagram Element Usage







    Context

    In the API development process, the method in the endpoint is invoked. An exception occurs during invocation. In this case, you need to add the exception capture diagram element to the diagram element orchestration so that the exception cause can be accurately located during API test.

    The process variable _exception is preset in the exception capture diagram element. The variable contains the _exception.name and _exception.cause. _exception.name indicates the name of an exception, and _exception.cause indicates the details of the exception.




    Usage Instruction


     Access the diagram element orchestration page of the Develop API.

     Add the service process based on the service logic. After the service process is added, add the exception diagram element handling process separately.

     Drag the exception diagram element, mapping diagram element, exclusive gateway diagram element, script diagram element, and connection branch to the canvas. Exclusive gateway diagram element: If there are multiple output flows, the first flow that meets the conditions can be used. If no flow meets the conditions, the default flow is used. Figure 1 shows an exception diagram element example.



       Figure 1 Exception diagram element example





     If the service side needs to customize process variables to receive exception information, you can add the mapping diagram element. Customize process variables in the diagram element and obtain required information from the _exception process variable.



       After adding the mapping diagram element, double-click and edit the diagram element to transfer the information obtained by the service customized exception class to _exception.name and _exception.cause, as shown in Figure 2. In addition, the service side can customize process variables to obtain the required information from _exception, for example, define exception_cause to receive the value of _exception.cause and add exception_class to receive the value of _exception.name.

        Figure 2 Editing the diagram element parameters





      Access the page for adding process variables and click the editing button, as shown in Figure 3. The _exception variable and its attribute values name and cause are preset process variables. The name and type cannot be changed and cannot be deleted. The attributes of the service in exception.cause can be extended.


       Figure 3 Adding a process variable



      You can obtain the customized error code or other customized information from the _exception.cause parameter. For example, if errorCode is defined for the exception class, you can obtain the definition from _exception.cause.errorCode.



     Based on the exception handling logic defined by the service, double-click the branch line to add a branch determination function.


      As shown in Figure 1, double-click branch 1 and branch 2 to edit their determination functions. The default branch does not need to be edited.


       As shown in Figure 4, after you double-click branch 1, the condition editing page is displayed. By default, there is a function. The determination logic is complete in the function. You can view the customized process variable on the left and drag it to the right for use.

        Figure 4 Editing a function





      Function example:

      (function(){
    if(exception_class == "com.huawei.usf.demo.sdl.MyException")
    {
        console.log("it is true;");
        return true;
    }
       console.log("it is false;");
        return false;
})();
      In the preceding information, exception_class is a customized process variable. If you do not use the datamapper diagram element to customize a process variable, you can use _exception.name to obtain the variable.



     Double-click the task diagram elements corresponding to branch 1, branch 2, and the default branch, and edit the processing scripts based on the service logic.

     After the configuration is complete, click Save.










