         Window function




           ROW_NUMBER(): indicates the row number.


           LAG(column, offset, default): indicates the previous offset value of the current column. If this parameter is invalid, the default value is used.




         select c, row_number() over (ORDER BY c) from (select 1 as c union all select 2 union all select 3) as t;
select c, lag(c, 1, 0) over (ORDER BY c) from (select 1 as c union all select 2 union all select 3) as t;
